  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Contact groups work without the MailboxItem permissions: in the default Contacts folder they are read, created, changed (name, notes, members) and deleted with SoftDelete through Microsoft Graph's distributionLists API, which needs only Contacts.Read or Contacts.ReadWrite. Graph does not show members that are directory distribution lists there, and a change it cannot store (categories, extended properties, another group as a member) returns an error that names the missing permission. With the MailboxItem permissions nothing changes. Online archives: Microsoft Graph no longer resolves the well-known folder names inside an archive, so the library now finds the archive's distinguished folders (archiveinbox, archivedeleteditems, the Recoverable Items folders) by their ids; in 2.3.0 they returned ErrorInvalidIdMalformed. Hidden folders of an archive, such as Files, now appear in FindFolder and SyncFolderHierarchy as in EWS, and pull subscriptions in an archive work again. An .eml saved as a received message works without MailboxItem.ImportExport.All too: with Mail-Advanced.ReadWrite.All it goes through Microsoft Graph's importMime and keeps the whole MIME, also an attached message, which before returned an error without the import permission.",
